so the nra the national rifle  association has filed for bankruptcy but  before you get your hopes up recognize  that this is  chapter 11 bankruptcy a chapter 11  bankruptcy is a kind of reorganization  that  attempts to pay off the creditors and  allow the  company or firm to continue as a going  forward concern now that being said it  can be used as a potential shield  against litigation or at least to delay  litigation and  the nra has filed for bankruptcy in  texas  probably seeking a more favorable venue  than new york where they're currently  being sued by  attorney general tish james who has  vowed to basically sue them  out of existence but it will be  interesting to see what happens here  because the nra is made up of many  different organizations  one of which the original is chartered  in new york but those assets may be  folded into some of the other nra  related affiliates so the nra is not  going anywhere at the moment  so stay tuned for more legal analysis  and i'll see you in court
 

